  :adr/body "## What moved

`cloud.itonami.app.appearance` (ADR-2608097000, ADR-0091) renders one
workspace in three appearances — `light` (DADS as shipped), `8bit`, `grok`.
Most of the file is data and mechanism the native word-typed slice
refuses by design: the palette maps, the CSS layers (`css` / `grok-css`),
the hiccup `toggle-button`, the `modes` vector, and the string PREPARATION
steps (`keyword?` / `name`, `str`, `str/trim`, `str/lower-case` — case
folding is not in the language, the ADR-2609081000 note on
`mail_domain_records`). All of that stays host.

What moves here are the three DECISIONS about plain strings:

    mode-of      :string -> [:option :string]
                 the `normalize` case table — which appearance a prepared
                 (trimmed, lower-cased) name denotes. The cljc's
                 `(case s (\"8bit\" \"8-bit\" \"eightbit\" \"eight-bit\"
                 \"pixel\" \"retro\") \"8bit\" ...)` group IS this function.

    next-of      :string -> :string
                 the toggle cycle — light -> 8bit -> grok -> light, with the
                 unknown-name fallback answering 8bit. The cljc's
                 keep-indexed/nth/mod formula over the `modes` vector IS this
                 function, and `(or (normalize mode) default-mode)` feeds the
                 canonical mode (or light) so the fallback matches i=0.

    plane-cloud? :string -> :bool
                 the residency judgement — is this prepared plane name
                 \\\"cloud\\\"? The cljc's `(= \\\"cloud\\\" s)` IS this predicate;
                 the host maps the boolean to the :cloud / :local keyword.

The host prepares (keyword->name, trim, lower-case) and routes on the
verdicts; `resolve-mode`'s `(or ... default-mode)` and `toggle-button`'s
label/title `case` stay host. Byte-faithful: a name the table does not
contain answers none, so `(or (normalize ...) default-mode)` reduces to the
default exactly as the old `case` produced; an unnormalizable toggle input
restarts the cycle from light exactly as the old index formula did.

## Nil discipline

A name the table does not contain answers none (mode-of) / false
(plane-cloud?) — never a throw and never a guessed mode. A guessed
appearance would render a mode the stylesheet does not define; the core
invents nothing (ADR-2609081000).

## Landed this tick

- `src/cloud/itonami/app/appearance_core.kotoba` — `mode-of`, `next-of`,
  `plane-cloud?`, all `if` / `string=?` limbs, no map
- `kotoba_oracle.cljc` `cores` gains `:appearance-core`
- `appearance.cljc` `normalize` / `next-mode` / `residency-plane` route
  through `kotoba-oracle`; the case table and the cycle formula are gone;
  prep, palettes, CSS, hiccup and `:cloud`/:local mapping stay host
- parity test `test/cloud/itonami/app/appearance_kotoba_parity_test.clj`
  + KIR regeneration + JVM-free gen_kir_amu identity

## Measured bounds on the pinned verifier (amu bin, jvm-free)

- `amu check src/cloud/itonami/app/appearance_core.kotoba --jvm-free` ->
  `:ok true, :effects #{}` (the authoritative gate; measured on the landed
  core)
- `if` / `string=?` with `:string` literals, `[:option :string]` results via
  `option-some-of` / `option-none-of`, and a `:bool` result -> admitted (the
  same vocabulary the option-argument cores and their parity probes already
  use)
- `str/trim` / `str/lower-case` / maps / vectors / hiccup do NOT cross the
  slice — that is why the host keeps them

## Status

Accepted. The 14-layer topo map (ADR-2609081000) lists `appearance` as a
layer-0 wave-0 candidate; measured 2026-09-08 by
`scripts/kotoba_slice_measure.py` against a fresh origin/main worktree
(`d3ce2cd`) it was the last remaining slice-ready wave-0 namespace (`amu`
gate off the whole-file check, by design — the file is data and mechanism;
the extracted core carries the decisions). The candidate was chosen from the
measure: sole candidate after `connectors` landed at ADR-2609081800. The
shared west checkout is pinned behind origin/main, so this tick again
measured against the fresh worktree and let its verdict stand."}]
